  { id: 'unvented-210', tier: 'Family homes', name: 'Unvented cylinder, 210 litres', price: '£1,695', from: true, unit: 'supplied and fitted, inc VAT',
    points: ['Suits 3 to 4 people', 'One bathroom, or a bath and en-suite shower', 'Expansion vessel and discharge pipe', 'Old cylinder taken away'] },
  { id: 'unvented-250', tier: 'Bigger homes', name: 'Unvented cylinder, 250 to 300 litres', price: '£1,995', from: true, unit: 'supplied and fitted, inc VAT',
    points: ['Suits 4 or more people', 'Two bathrooms used at once', 'Mains pressure at every tap', 'Free survey to confirm the size'] },
];

const faqs = [
  { q: 'How much does a hot water cylinder cost on the Wirral?', a: 'A vented cylinder replaced starts from £750 including VAT. An unvented cylinder starts from £1,450 for 150 litres, £1,695 for 210 litres and £1,995 for 250 to 300 litres. Changing from vented to unvented starts from £1,895. You get a fixed written price after a free survey.' },
  { q: 'Do you cover all Wirral CH postcodes?', a: 'Yes. We cover the whole Wirral, from CH41 Birkenhead to CH64 Neston. That includes Wallasey, Moreton, Hoylake, West Kirby, Heswall, Bebington and Bromborough. The price is the same in every CH postcode, with no call-out fee.' },
  { q: 'Do I need a new cylinder if my loft conversion removes the cold water tank?', a: 'Yes, if your hot water comes from a vented cylinder fed by that tank. Without the tank, the old cylinder cannot work. The usual answer is an unvented cylinder fed from the mains. A change from vented to unvented starts from £1,895.' },
  { q: 'Can you work around my loft conversion builder?', a: 'Yes. We agree with your builder when the tank comes out and when the new cylinder goes in. That way you are not left without hot water for long.' },
  { q: 'We are adding an en-suite in Heswall. Will our cylinder cope?', a: 'Often not, if it is vented. A loft tank system struggles when two showers run at once. An unvented cylinder gives mains pressure to both. We check your mains pressure and flow at the free survey first.' },
  { q: 'Are your engineers G3 qualified?', a: 'Yes. All our engineers are G3 qualified to fit and service unvented cylinders. The work is notified as the Building Regulations require, and you get the paperwork to keep.' },
  { q: 'How long does a cylinder swap take?', a: 'Most swaps are done in one day. A change from vented to unvented, or a tight airing cupboard, can take a little longer. We tell you at the survey.' },
  { q: 'How much is a new immersion heater on the Wirral?', a: 'An immersion heater on a vented cylinder is £175 including VAT. On an unvented cylinder it is £275. Both are supplied and fitted, and are often done the same day.' },
  { q: 'Does an unvented cylinder need a yearly service?', a: 'Yes. Makers ask for a yearly service to keep the warranty valid. It also checks the safety valves still work. Our unvented cylinder service is £120 including VAT.' },
  { q: 'Are you Gas Safe registered?', a: 'Yes. Gas work is done by our Gas Safe registered engineers. You can check any engineer on the Gas Safe Register before they start.' },
];
